        "class": "view-mode-section view-mode-section__branch view-mode-section__branch--human"
      },
      "html": "<div class=\"w-full bg-chalk\"><section class=\"blog-reading-shell pointer-events-auto\" data-v-1c6297c3><nav class=\"blog-breadcrumb\" aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\"><a href=\"/feed\">Blogs</a><span aria-hidden=\"true\">/</span><span>AI search visibility</span></nav><article aria-labelledby=\"blog-36-title\"><header class=\"blog-article-header\"><p class=\"blog-eyebrow\">Search &amp; AI Visibility</p><h1 id=\"blog-36-title\">Make your business information consistent for AI discovery</h1><p class=\"blog-article-summary\">Give customers and discovery systems a consistent account of your services, contact details, markets and supporting evidence.</p><p class=\"blog-byline\">Fyntix Editorial · Updated <time datetime=\"2026-11-24\">24 Nov 2026</time> · 2 min read</p></header><nav class=\"blog-contents\" aria-label=\"On this page\"><p>On this page</p><ol><li><a href=\"#blog-36-section-1\">Create an approved business description</a></li><li><a href=\"#blog-36-section-2\">Review the important public surfaces</a></li><li><a href=\"#blog-36-section-3\">Keep evidence attached to its context</a></li><li><a href=\"#blog-36-section-4\">Observe representation without overclaiming control</a></li></ol></nav><div class=\"blog-prose\"><p>A business can be described differently across its website, profiles, directory listings and older articles. Customers may encounter any of those descriptions while researching a service. Inconsistency creates uncertainty about what the business does and which information is current.</p>\n<p>Begin with the information your own team can confirm. A clear, maintained source makes it easier to improve pages and identify outdated descriptions elsewhere. The task is information quality, with a practical role in both human and AI-assisted discovery.</p>\n<h2 id=\"blog-36-section-1\">Create an approved business description</h2>\n<p>Describe the company, its services, intended customers and actual markets. Include contact details and the next step for someone who wants help. Avoid broad claims that the business cannot explain or support.</p>\n<p>For example, a company offering local services should distinguish its office location from its service coverage. Those details answer different questions and should remain accurate wherever they appear.</p>\n<h2 id=\"blog-36-section-2\">Review the important public surfaces</h2>\n<p>Compare the main website pages with the profiles and listings customers are likely to use. Identify outdated offers, inconsistent names and contact routes that no longer work. Prioritise sources the business controls or can reasonably request to update.</p>\n<p>Record the owner and review date for each important surface. Consistency becomes easier to maintain when updates have a process, rather than relying on someone remembering every place the company is mentioned.</p>\n<h2 id=\"blog-36-section-3\">Keep evidence attached to its context</h2>\n<p>Case studies, examples and specialist explanations should preserve their meaning when reused. A result needs its measure and reporting period. A service claim needs enough detail to help a reader assess fit. Avoid turning qualified information into a universal promise.</p>\n<p>This matters when preparing concise summaries for different channels. Shorter wording should still reflect the underlying service accurately, with a route to fuller information for people who need it.</p>\n<h2 id=\"blog-36-section-4\">Observe representation without overclaiming control</h2>\n<p>Review relevant customer questions and record how the business is described in the experiences you are investigating. Note inaccurate information and the sources that can be inspected. Keep mentions and citations separate from visits or enquiries in the report.</p>\n<p>Fyntix's Search &amp; AI Visibility work connects content structure, business information and useful expertise. Maintaining a consistent account of the company gives that work a dependable foundation, while acknowledging that external platforms control how information appears in their own results and answers.</p></div><aside class=\"blog-service-callout\" aria-label=\"Work with Fyntix\"><p class=\"blog-eyebrow\">Put the idea into practice</p><h2>Plan your next step with Fyntix.</h2><p>Connect your audience and offer with a practical plan for search visibility, paid media and useful content.</p><div class=\"blog-callout-links\"><a href=\"/contact\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-full\">Book a free strategy call</a><a href=\"/services#service-ai-search-visibility\">Explore the relevant service</a></div></aside></article></section></div>"
